# Local profile: one operator, no proxy, reached at 127.0.0.1 only. Never tunnel,
# forward or publish this. Local mode is host-loopback only: it rejects DASHBOARD_ORIGIN,
# CF_ACCESS_* and DASHBOARD_OWNER outright and requires DASHBOARD_BIND=127.0.0.1, so this
# profile runs the app directly on the host and never inside a container — a container must
# bind its own interface, which requires hosted mode with container-private-interface
# (see env.hosted.example).
DASHBOARD_MODE=local
DASHBOARD_EXPOSURE=host-loopback
DASHBOARD_BIND=127.0.0.1
PORT=4319
# A host path owned by the account that runs this profile (the systemd unit's user), not the
# container's /data volume (that belongs to the hosted profile). systemd's EnvironmentFile does
# not expand variables, so give an absolute path under that account's home — for example
# /home/<user>/.local/share/pilot-data — and make sure that directory exists and is writable by it.
DASHBOARD_DATA=/home/<user>/.local/share/pilot-data
# How many model requests one dispatch may make in a row before it stops for review. Default 8.
# DASHBOARD_MAX_MODEL_TURNS=40
# Enable bounded file-edit capability for agents with the file_edit scope (default off).
# DASHBOARD_FILE_EDIT=on

# Enable the agent commit tool (default: off). Set to 'on' to install `commit_preview` and
# `commit_accepted` for agents with the commit scope, with a control store, an owner-configured
# commit target and an agent-may-accept policy whose commit decision is full-auto. It commits the
# exact staged tree to the fixed Pilot branch and never pushes; staging is not secret scanning.
# DASHBOARD_AGENT_COMMIT=on
# Enable the agent push tool (default: off). Set to 'on' to install `push_preview` and
# `push_accepted` for agents with the push scope, with a control store, an owner-configured push
# target and the same full-auto policy requirement. It pushes one accepted commit, without force,
# to one locally configured filesystem remote; there is no hosted credential integration.
# DASHBOARD_AGENT_PUSH=on
# Enable the owner-only Cloudflare connection configuration route (default off). It stores one
# unencrypted credential in credentials/ and makes no provider request or deployment; removing it
# here does not revoke it at Cloudflare. See docs/specs/cloudflare-connection-store.md.
# DASHBOARD_CLOUDFLARE_CONNECTION=on
# Enable the coding tools `read` and `write` for agents with file_read/file_write (default off).
# DASHBOARD_CODING_TOOLS=on
# Enable the `bash` tool for agents with the shell scope (default off, needs the line above).
# The shell is NOT contained: it runs as the application user and can reach every project, the
# durable store and credentials/. Grant the shell scope only where that is intended.
# DASHBOARD_SHELL=on

# Enable the local test-execution capability (default off). With this on, a named agent bound to a
# session and granted the run_tests scope can run the fixed `node --test` recipe in the registered
# project root. It runs as the application user inside the application container and is NOT a
# sandbox: the tests can read credentials/, the durable control store and every project, and can
# modify this project. There are no cgroup memory or PID limits, and stopping a run is a best-effort
# process-group signal. See docs/RUNNER.md.
# DASHBOARD_TEST_RUNNER=on

# Enable the opt-in reusable JSON projection tools (default: off). An owner must also grant the
# 'reusable_tools' scope to a bound named agent. Definitions are bounded data, never code, and
# nothing is executed. See docs/specs/reusable-json-tools.md.
# DASHBOARD_REUSABLE_TOOLS=on
